Upstream: Qt
------------
ferrokit re-implements parts of the design, the algorithms and the observable behaviour of Qt
(https://github.com/qt/qtbase). Comments in the source point at the qtbase files and lines that a
behaviour was checked against. Those line numbers refer to one checkout of the qtbase 6.11 branch
(commit 44b6f67476c34716061e9eddcbffcbfcb4cb7842; its .cmake.conf says version 6.11.3 with the
pre-release segment alpha1, so it is not the 6.11.3 release) and differ between Qt versions. They
were not compared with any Qt release, except that qobject.cpp:2309-2345 was also compared with
the Qt 6.11.2 tag. Qt is available under several licenses, among them the LGPL-3.0-only that
ferrokit uses.

The qtbase files referred to carry the copyright of The Qt Company Ltd. and, in some files, of
other contributors, among them Intel Corporation, Klaralvdalens Datakonsult AB (a KDAB Group
company), Olivier Goffart, Samuel Gaist and Konstantin Ritt. The header of each upstream file has
its exact notices. This list is not exhaustive.

Of the 11 qcocoa* files of qtbase that ferrokit's macOS code refers to, four are licensed under the
BSD 3-Clause license (LICENSES/BSD-3-Clause.txt); the other seven carry Qt's usual set of licenses,
which includes LGPL-3.0-only (checked in the qtbase checkout named above):

